# Every eval/load run writes a timestamped report, so these pile up fast. One
# representative result per test type is committed as evidence for the numbers
# quoted in README.md; new runs stay local. (Files already tracked are
# unaffected by these rules — this only stops future ones being added.)
load_test_results/*.json
scoring_eval_results/*.json
adversarial_results/*.json
